---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro'
import { URLS } from '../config'
---

<LegalPage
  title="Abuse and takedowns"
  description="How to report abuse on Telium: who can act, and how to reach them."
  updated="2026-11-13"
>
  <p>
    Telium has no central authority. The people who can actually remove content or
    suspend an account are the <strong>operators of the servers it lives on</strong>.
    telium.chat hosts only a website and a directory, so we cannot delete messages,
    accounts or files on anyone's server. Reporting to the right place is what gets
    things done.
  </p>

  <h2>If you are in Telium</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Report a message</strong> from its menu. Your home server forwards the report,
      with a copy of the message as evidence, to the server of the person who wrote it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Tell the guild's moderators</strong> as well. Moderators can remove the content
      from the guild, which a report to the author's server cannot do.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Block the person</strong> to stop seeing them while you wait.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>If you are outside Telium</h2>
  <p>
    Find the server's domain: in a Telium address <code>@name:domain</code> it is the part
    after the colon. Servers listed in the <a href={URLS.servers}>directory</a> must give an
    operator contact that reaches a person. For other servers, look for a contact on the
    server's own website, or ask its administrators in a guild hosted there. Send the operator
    the address of the content, what is wrong with it and,
    if the law requires it, the legal basis for your request.
  </p>

  <h2>What we can do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Hide or remove a directory listing for a server that ignores serious abuse reports.
      Report that on <a href={URLS.github}>GitHub</a>.
    </li>
    <li>Pass a report to the right operator if you can't tell who that is.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Emergencies and illegal content</h2>
  <p>
    If someone is in immediate danger, contact local emergency services, not a chat server.
    For child sexual abuse material, report it to your national hotline or police as
    well as the operator. Do not copy or forward the material itself.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
